# LRT Engineering Rules for AI & Developers

1. NEVER create or ask for text documentation files (e.g., ARCHITECTURE.md, TZ.md, DESIGN.md, ADR-*.md).
2. The Single Source of Truth (SoT) for business invariants is `tests/contracts/*_test.go`. Always run `task test:contracts` to verify domain logic.
3. The SoT for domain states, enums, and models is the PostgreSQL schema (`db/migrations`) and types generated by `sqlc`. Never use raw string literals for states in Go code.
4. Only README.md (local setup) and DEPLOY.md (CI/CD) are permitted as prose documentation on disk.
5. Every refactoring or feature MUST start with an updated contract in `tests/contracts/` that fails (RED) before implementation (GREEN).
6. Product identity and all env/design/infra/tooling/HTTP/app-face/landing literals live in `internal/tokens`. Regenerate derived files with `task tokens:gen` (`.env.example`, `web/tokens.css`, `docker-compose.yml`, `sqlc.yaml`, `Dockerfile`, `web/app/face.html`, `.cursor/rules/lrt.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/vitek-policy.mdc`). Never edit those by hand.
7. Multi-tenant Avito SaaS platform (multiple product services). First shipped service = listing_search; other services (e.g. listing warmup) are reserved, not built yet. Domains: landing vitek.tech (magic link only), platform app.vitek.tech (USER + ADMIN shell). HTTP surface = `tokens.HTTP*Routes` policy only; anything else → 404. Auth = Magic Link (HTTP request/consume/logout + sessions). Avito accounts + proxies CRUD via admin HTTP; live lists UI later when contracted. listing_search processors: stub | avito (HTTP JSON) | rod (Chrome SERP, filter URLs only; ROD_USER_DATA_DIR). Chrome-in-worker image — later when contracted. Telegram / Redis / feed matcher — later only when contracted. Do not add packages or deps ahead of contracts.
8. Commit messages that change invariants MUST include an `LRT-VERIFY:` block naming the contract file and GREEN status.
9. Keep Day-0 surface minimal: no empty packages, no docs that describe missing artifacts, no unused infra (compose/env/deps) without a consumer + contract.
10. Transport (internal/transport) must NOT import internal/repository directly — use internal/service (CONTRACT-ARCH-001).
